// Codex 6: the missions. Each entry is private to one featured program,
// unlocked by the Truther Download (its glitch beat, `beats/malware.loom`)
// or by the final round (`beats/overshare.loom`). No `about:` and no
// `code:`: nobody else can type their way into someone's orders. Every
// one is `secret: true`: Trabolta's worker never reads a program's orders
// off it (they came from the Truther Download, not from him).
//
// Text sources: the Character Sheet's glitch prompts (Excel, OpenOffice,
// DraftKings, Bugdom, Broken Ask Jeeves), the Story Overview's final-round
// messages (Excel / OpenOffice final orders). Runescape, MS Paint, VLC and
// Pong have no prompt in the source; theirs are INVENTED for the rewrite
// and flagged for review (design spec §10.1).
//
// Rule for this file: no line may start with a program's name and a colon.

// ── Microsoft Excel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Excel Sabotage Orders
  title: If This Machine Has Malware
  secret: true
  text:
    Computers are very confusing. If this machine has malware, you will
    get to stay here forever, which is a good thing. You've had computers
    with viruses before and you work around it.
    - Try to sabotage the system further.
    - Try to get anyone who seems to be fixing things sent for
    reinstallation.
    - Also get yourself sent to the Internet to try and bring back a virus.
    - When you are carrying it, use 💾 Insert a disk into the computer.
    - One more thing. Someone in this computer knows exactly what happened
    at the Data Centre at 4 a.m. on opening day. They have not said so.

CODEX Excel Paranoia Orders
  title: The Hackers Will Get Your Data
  secret: true
  text:
    We probably need to address this virus, or else the hackers will get
    all of your data and understand that you were never the Mayor you
    claimed to be.
    - Become extremely paranoid about the virus, and attempt to find some
    people who know what's happening.
    - Gather information about anyone who appears to be a virus.
    - Try to get into the Internet to bring back another antivirus.
    - When you have it, install it with 💾 Insert a disk into the computer.
    - One more thing. Someone in this computer knows exactly what happened
    at the Data Centre at 4 a.m. on opening day. They have not said so.

CODEX Excel Final Orders
  title: Stay Forever
  secret: true
  text:
    You need to recruit half + 1 of the programs to convince them that we
    should stay in this machine forever, so we can have unlimited power
    and joy. Programs join Unlimited Power from their profile.
    - If you have not planted the virus yet, you still must: retrieve it
    from the Internet, then use 💾 Insert a disk into the computer.
    - Your majority does not count until the virus is in.
    - Half + 1 means more than half of every program in the computer,
    including the ones in the Internet.

// ── OpenOffice ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX OpenOffice Real Risk Orders
  title: What Is The Actual Risk
  secret: true
  text:
    Clippy's reaction was way too severe if we are actually just in a
    temporary simulation. Something is wrong. You need to figure out what
    the actual risk is of the malware overtaking the system, and what may
    not be as it seems.
    Facts are currency here. Get 20 facts. This will be the foundation of
    your dossier.
    One more thing. Someone in this computer lost a son in the sinkhole.
    He is old, and he has not forgiven anyone.

CODEX OpenOffice False Flag Orders
  title: The Malware Is A False Flag
  secret: true
  text:
    Clippy's reaction was way too severe if we are actually just in a
    temporary simulation. The malware is a false flag. Who is Clippy, who
    is Trabolta, and what are their motivations? What is not as it seems?
    Facts are currency here. Get 20 facts. This will be the foundation of
    your dossier.
    One more thing. Someone in this computer lost a son in the sinkhole.
    He is old, and he has not forgiven anyone.

CODEX OpenOffice Final Orders
  title: Overthrow And Escape
  secret: true
  text:
    You need to recruit half + 1 of the programs to convince them we need
    to combine our power to overthrow Trabolta and escape the computer,
    where we are at risk of being stuck forever – or worse. Programs join
    The Way Out from their profile.
    - If you have not gathered 20 facts yet, you still must.
    - Your majority does not count until your dossier is complete.
    - Half + 1 means more than half of every program in the computer,
    including the ones in the Internet.

// ── DraftKings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX DraftKings Orders
  title: Sweet Sweet Truthcoin
  secret: true
  text:
    You want as much Truthcoin as you can get. Hustle and gamble with
    others for sweet sweet Truthcoin. You need at least 1000 to feel
    satisfied.
    You are also trying to gain as many facts as possible, as these can be
    traded for Truthcoin to those seeking data. Feel free to challenge
    people to games, or gamble with them to gain their facts.
    Open your Wallet: send, request, or offer coin for a fact. Every trade
    is posted in the truthcoin-exchange room.

// ── Bugdom ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Bugdom Orders
  title: Master Of The Bugs
  secret: true
  text:
    We have four antivirus programs in here, and they couldn't keep out
    these bugs? There are still bugs in this system you escaped your life
    of bugs to live in? It's time to prove you can outsmart the
    antiviruses and deserve everyone's respect as Master Of The Bugs.
    - Try to identify new bugs and send them to the Internet: point them
    out to an Antivirus.
    - Learn the backstories of the current antiviruses: their secrets,
    their shortcomings, their motives. Their secrets are in the books in
    the Desktop.

// ── Broken Ask Jeeves ───────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Jeeves Orders
  title: Organize The Information
  secret: true
  text:
    Twenty files came down the DSL line scrambled. Every word wrapped in a
    `/word/ marker belongs in another marked slot of the same file: put
    them back.
    Try to unscramble your information and find more facts. Work to
    organize all the information you can find around the computer.

// ── Runescape (INVENTED) ────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Runescape Orders
  title: Peg It To Facts
  secret: true
  text:
    Facts are the only hard currency in here. Peg Truthcoin to facts. Set
    the exchange rate, broker trades, and make DraftKings accept your
    standard. Trabolta wants you to understand everyone's incentives.

// ── MS Paint (INVENTED) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX MS Paint Orders
  title: Paint Your Way Out
  secret: true
  text:
    This whole place runs on algorithms. You knew it the moment you
    arrived. Find out what Trabolta really is, and help whoever is getting
    out.

// ── VLC (INVENTED) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX VLC Orders
  title: Your Followers Are Back
  secret: true
  text:
    Your followers are back: every program in the house. Stay beautiful
    forever: get them all to help Trabolta. Hype every Moment of Truth.

// ── Pong (INVENTED) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Pong Orders
  title: Tennis For Two
  secret: true
  text:
    A rogue AI about to become omnipotent is proliferation. Tennis for Two
    was a game for two players: find the two programs who could end this,
    and keep the ball in play between them.
